const wineNarrative = {
  eyebrow: 'WINE CELLAR COOLING — THE CATEGORY NOBODY SERVICES',
  headline: 'A Wine Room Is a Refrigeration System, Not a Fancy Fridge',
  paragraphs: [
    "Search for wine cellar cooling repair in San Diego and you'll find companies that sell wine coolers — the undercounter kind — and almost nobody who services the systems behind real cellars. La Jolla has real cellars: converted lower-level rooms in the Muirlands, purpose-built collector spaces in the Farms, conditioned closets in Village remodels. When one drifts from 55 toward 60, the owner discovers that the installer retired and the appliance companies don't want the call.",
    "We want the call. A cellar system is a refrigeration loop plus everything around it: the through-wall or ducted cooling unit, the condenser's airflow supply (usually starved in an equipment closet nobody opens), the evaporator side's humidity behavior (a cellar that dries corks is failing even at the right temperature), and the room itself — insulation, vapor barrier, door seal. Half the 'failing cooling units' we see are healthy machines suffocating in a closed closet or fighting a door that no longer seals. The other half need real refrigeration work, and we hold EPA 608 Universal certification for exactly that.",
    "A cellar visit here follows a fixed discipline. Temperatures logged at rack level, not just at the thermostat — stratification is real in tall rooms. Condenser airflow measured where the unit actually breathes, which in most La Jolla installs means a closet, a crawl space, or a cabinet toe-kick that hasn't seen a vacuum since the remodel. Evaporator inspected for icing, drain line for the algae plug that coastal humidity grows, door seal checked with the lights-off test. Then, and only then, refrigerant questions — because condemning a compressor before ruling out airflow is how cellars end up with two expensive repairs instead of one cheap one. You get the findings in writing either way.",
    "We service dedicated cellar cooling units, through-wall and split systems, and the undercounter and column wine refrigeration from Sub-Zero, EuroCave, Liebherr, and U-Line that backs up the main room. Temperature drift, short cycling, humidity complaints, ice on the evaporator — diagnosed as a system, quoted in writing before work starts. If your collection is sitting in a warming room right now, say so when you call and we'll schedule it with the urgency a cellar actually deserves."
